% Test cases for the tremor stimulator policy (tremor_stimulator.le):
% synthetic claims, one per criterion of LCD L39591 and its
% continued-coverage rule, each stating only what its record shows. The
% findings are recorded as the treating practitioner's, a medical
% reviewer's or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the answer
% conditional. The queries: whether the claim is payable (the first query,
% so "stage" reads its checklist), whether it is reasonable and necessary,
% and what minimal change would make it payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base tremor stimulator cases includes these resources:
    tremor_stimulator.

the knowledge base tremor stimulator cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month claim for a tremor stimulator (E0734): the
% evaluation, the eight criteria, the standard written order, the delivery
% and its proof.
scenario initial_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the tremor stimulator.
    the HCPCS code of the tremor stimulator is "E0734".
    the tremor stimulator is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ann had a clinical evaluation in person or via telehealth by the treating practitioner on 2026-02-10.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "G25.0".
    the age of Ann is 72 years.
    the finding free of contraindications about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the tremor stimulator is prescribed to treat the dominant upper limb of Ann.
    the BF-ADL score of Ann for eating before therapy is 4.
    the BF-ADL score of Ann for writing before therapy is 3.
    the finding tremor exacerbating medications addressed about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "the albuterol inhaler was replaced by an anticholinergic".
    2 pharmacological treatment options for essential tremor were tried and failed or ruled out for Ann.
    the tremor stimulator is prescribed as an alternative to invasive or permanent surgical treatment for Ann.
    the order for the tremor stimulator is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the tremor stimulator is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the tremor stimulator includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the tremor stimulator includes order date.
    the order for the tremor stimulator includes description of the item.
    the order for the tremor stimulator includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the tremor stimulator includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the tremor stimulator was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the tremor stimulator was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the tremor stimulator.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% Criteria 1 and 2 fail: a 17 year old (claim 1), and a tremor coded
% outside Group 1 — G25.2, other specified forms of tremor (claim 2).
scenario age_and_diagnosis is:
    claim 1 is for the first stimulator.
    the HCPCS code of the first stimulator is "E0734".
    the first stimulator is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Ben had a clinical evaluation in person or via telehealth by the treating practitioner on 2026-02-10.
    the diagnosis code of Ben is "G25.0".
    the age of Ben is 17 years.
    the finding free of contraindications about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the first stimulator is prescribed to treat the dominant upper limb of Ben.
    the BF-ADL score of Ben for eating before therapy is 4.
    the finding tremor exacerbating medications addressed about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "no exacerbating medication is taken".
    2 pharmacological treatment options for essential tremor were tried and failed or ruled out for Ben.
    the first stimulator is prescribed as an alternative to invasive or permanent surgical treatment for Ben.
    claim 2 is for the second stimulator.
    the HCPCS code of the second stimulator is "E0734".
    the second stimulator is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    Cy had a clinical evaluation in person or via telehealth by the treating practitioner on 2026-02-10.
    the diagnosis code of Cy is "G25.2".
    the age of Cy is 70 years.
    the finding free of contraindications about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the second stimulator is prescribed to treat the dominant upper limb of Cy.
    the BF-ADL score of Cy for drinking before therapy is 3.
    the finding tremor exacerbating medications addressed about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "no exacerbating medication is taken".
    3 pharmacological treatment options for essential tremor were tried and failed or ruled out for Cy.
    the second stimulator is prescribed as an alternative to invasive or permanent surgical treatment for Cy.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Criterion 5 fails: no upper limb item scored 3 or more (a 3 on walking
% up and down stairs is not an upper limb item).
scenario mild_tremor is:
    claim 1 is for the tremor stimulator.
    the HCPCS code of the tremor stimulator is "E0734".
    the tremor stimulator is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Dee had a clinical evaluation in person or via telehealth by the treating practitioner on 2026-02-10.
    the diagnosis code of Dee is "G25.0".
    the age of Dee is 68 years.
    the finding free of contraindications about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the tremor stimulator is prescribed to treat the dominant upper limb of Dee.
    the BF-ADL score of Dee for eating before therapy is 2.
    the BF-ADL score of Dee for writing before therapy is 2.
    the BF-ADL score of Dee for stairs before therapy is 3.
    the finding tremor exacerbating medications addressed about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "no exacerbating medication is taken".
    2 pharmacological treatment options for essential tremor were tried and failed or ruled out for Dee.
    the tremor stimulator is prescribed as an alternative to invasive or permanent surgical treatment for Dee.
    rn expects answers [].

% Criterion 7 fails: one pharmacological option tried, not two.
scenario one_drug_tried is:
    claim 1 is for the tremor stimulator.
    the HCPCS code of the tremor stimulator is "E0734".
    the tremor stimulator is furnished to Eve.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Eve had a clinical evaluation in person or via telehealth by the treating practitioner on 2026-02-10.
    the diagnosis code of Eve is "G25.0".
    the age of Eve is 75 years.
    the finding free of contraindications about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the tremor stimulator is prescribed to treat the dominant upper limb of Eve.
    the BF-ADL score of Eve for self care before therapy is 4.
    the finding tremor exacerbating medications addressed about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "no exacerbating medication is taken".
    1 pharmacological treatment options for essential tremor were tried and failed or ruled out for Eve.
    the tremor stimulator is prescribed as an alternative to invasive or permanent surgical treatment for Eve.
    rn expects answers [].

% Criterion 3, a Council-style finding: the medical reviewer finds the
% record of an implanted cardiac pacemaker, a contraindication the
% practitioner's note did not address.
scenario contraindication_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the tremor stimulator.
    the HCPCS code of the tremor stimulator is "E0734".
    the tremor stimulator is furnished to Fay.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Fay had a clinical evaluation in person or via telehealth by the treating practitioner on 2026-02-10.
    the diagnosis code of Fay is "G25.0".
    the age of Fay is 80 years.
    the finding free of contraindications about Fay is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the hospital records document an implanted cardiac pacemaker, which the treating practitioner's note does not mention".
    the tremor stimulator is prescribed to treat the dominant upper limb of Fay.
    the BF-ADL score of Fay for eating before therapy is 4.
    the finding tremor exacerbating medications addressed about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "no exacerbating medication is taken".
    2 pharmacological treatment options for essential tremor were tried and failed or ruled out for Fay.
    the tremor stimulator is prescribed as an alternative to invasive or permanent surgical treatment for Fay.
    rn expects answers [].

% Month 4: re-evaluated on day 75 with the eating score improved from 4 to
% 2 and 80 percent adherence — the device (claim 1) and a wrist band
% (A4542, claim 2) 92 days into therapy.
scenario month_4_benefit is:
    claim 1 is for the tremor stimulator.
    the HCPCS code of the tremor stimulator is "E0734".
    the tremor stimulator is furnished to Gus.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-06-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    claim 2 is for the wrist band.
    the HCPCS code of the wrist band is "A4542".
    the wrist band is an accessory of the tremor stimulator.
    the wrist band is furnished to Gus.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-06-01.
    Gus had a clinical evaluation in person or via telehealth by the treating practitioner on 2026-02-10.
    the diagnosis code of Gus is "G25.0".
    the age of Gus is 66 years.
    the finding free of contraindications about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the tremor stimulator is prescribed to treat the dominant upper limb of Gus.
    the BF-ADL score of Gus for eating before therapy is 4.
    the BF-ADL score of Gus for writing before therapy is 2.
    the finding tremor exacerbating medications addressed about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "no exacerbating medication is taken".
    2 pharmacological treatment options for essential tremor were tried and failed or ruled out for Gus.
    the tremor stimulator is prescribed as an alternative to invasive or permanent surgical treatment for Gus.
    the tremor stimulator was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    Gus had a clinical re-evaluation in person or via telehealth by the treating practitioner on 2026-05-15.
    the BF-ADL score of Gus for eating at the re-evaluation is 2.
    the BF-ADL score of Gus for writing at the re-evaluation is 1.
    Gus used the tremor stimulator on 80 percent of the days during a consecutive thirty day period within the first three months.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

